.TH REGISTRY-RUST 1 "January 2026" "registry-rust" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
registry-rust \- OCI/Docker registry server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B registry-rust
.RI [OPTIONS] " server"
.br
.B registry-rust
.RI [OPTIONS] " check-config"
.br
.B registry-rust
.RI [OPTIONS] " ref-index " "check|ensure|rebuild"
.br
.B registry-rust
.RI [OPTIONS] " blob-gc " "plan|quarantine|delete" " [--policy ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B registry-rust
is a lightweight OCI/Docker registry implementation in Rust.
.PP
For the full CLI and configuration options, run:
.PP
.B registry-rust --help
.PP
Maintenance commands:
.TP
.B registry-rust ref-index check|ensure|rebuild
Inspect/rebuild the persistent blob reference index.
.TP
.B registry-rust blob-gc plan|quarantine|delete
Reclaim disk space by quarantining/deleting unreferenced blobs (filesystem backend only).

.PP
Note: for safety, these maintenance commands refuse to run while a live
registry server is active on the same filesystem root.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/registry-rust/registry.core.toml
Core configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/registry-rust/registry.auth.toml
Authentication/authorization configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/default/registry-rust
Environment overrides for the systemd service.
.SH SEE ALSO
systemd(1)
